#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The B<getusershell>()  function returns the next line from the file I</etc/"
"shells>, opening the file if necessary.  The line should contain the "
"pathname of a valid user shell.  If I</etc/shells> does not exist or is "
"unreadable, B<getusershell>()  behaves as if I</bin/sh> and I</bin/csh> were "
"listed in the file."
msgstr ""
"La función B<getusershell>() devuelve la siguiente línea del fichero I</etc/"
"shells>, abriéndolo si es necesario.  La línea debería contener la ruta de "
"una shell de usuario válida. Si I</etc/shells> no existe o no se puede leer, "
"B<getusershell>() se comporta como si en el fichero se encontraran las "
"shells I</bin/sh> y I</bin/csh>."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The B<setusershell>()  function rewinds I</etc/shells>."
msgstr "La función B<setusershell>() reinicializa I</etc/shells>."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The B<endusershell>()  function closes I</etc/shells>."
msgstr "La función B<endusershell>() cierra I</etc/shells>."

